$$
48 + 6 = 54
$$

Now, the coach wants to divide these 54 players into groups where each group has **6 players**. To find out how many such groups can be formed, we divide the total number of players by the number of players per group:

$$
54 \div 6 = 9
$$

This division tells us that 9 groups of 6 players each can be formed. There is no remainder, so all players are evenly divided into groups.

Therefore, the number of groups is:

$$
\boxed{9}
